- op: create  # 7845
  at: '2026-09-22T08:39:44Z'  # 7845
  by: agent  # 7845
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7845
  clock: 1  # 7845
  nonce: '7845'  # 7845
  data:  # 7845
    kind: work_item  # 7845
    title: "A walk that was never attempted publishes as ddg_mixed: WI-ripas made that population large enough to matter"  # 7845
    status: todo_hard  # 7845
    priority: 3  # 7845
    parent:  # 7845
    tags: []  # 7845
    isbefore: []  # 7845
    duplicate_of: []  # 7845
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 7845
    pr_ref:  # 7845
    description: "`method_for_walk_verdict` (taint.py:408) maps the three-valued walk result onto\nthe published `analysis_method` vocabulary:\n\n    confirmed    -> ddg\n    unavailable  -> structural\n    EVERYTHING ELSE, including not_attempted and escaped -> ddg_mixed\n\nIts docstring states the collapse is deliberate: \"three verdicts share\nddg_mixed, which is precisely the collapse INV-zidur exists to make visible\nWITHOUT changing what the coarse name means to an existing consumer.\" INV-zidur\n(satisfied) added `walk_verdict` as the finer axis rather than adding a fourth\n`analysis_method` value, and explicitly declined to invalidate published uses of\n`ddg_mixed`.\n\nWHAT WI-ripas CHANGED ABOUT THE STAKES. Before it, a python METHOD could never\nhave `fn_has_ddg` true, so its findings were `unavailable` -> `structural`.\nAfter it, the same findings reach the walk machinery -- and where the walk is\nnever attempted, they land on `not_attempted` -> `ddg_mixed`.\n\nMEASURED 2026-09-22, podman-compose under generic-taint-claims.yaml with\n--include-non-production-sources (an arm that is 100% method-rooted):\n\n    before   analysis_method {structural 7}    walk {unavailable 7}\n    after    analysis_method {ddg_mixed 7, ddg 1}\n             walk {not_attempted 6, escaped 1, confirmed 1}\n\nSo SIX OF EIGHT findings now read as `ddg_mixed` with NO WALK EVER ATTEMPTED.\nThey earned a DDG-flavoured label from DDG COVERAGE, not from any walk result.\nA reader of `analysis_method` alone cannot tell that from a walk that ran and\nestablished nothing, which is the same one-name-two-facts shape INV-zidur was\nfiled about -- now reached from the other side.\n\nTHE QUESTION, which is an owner decision because it touches a published\nvocabulary: should a finding whose walk was NOT ATTEMPTED read as `ddg_mixed`?\n\nOptions, none of them free:\n  (a) Leave it. `ddg_mixed` already means \"the DDG covered the function\", which\n      is TRUE here, and INV-zidur deliberately preserved that meaning. Cost:\n      the coarse name keeps carrying a fact the reader will misread as\n      evidence, and WI-ripas just made that population much larger.\n  (b) Map not_attempted -> structural. Keeps the exclusion semantics readers\n      expect. Cost: `structural` then means two different things (no DDG data\n      at all, vs DDG data present but the walk never ran), which is the defect\n      being fixed, mirrored.\n  (c) A fourth analysis_method value. INV-zidur explicitly REFUSED this --\n      \"folding a verdict into a method name repeats the one-name-two-facts\n      shape being fixed\" -- and it would invalidate published uses of\n      ddg_mixed in docs/measurements/0006 and docs/VERIFY-CLAIMS-SCOPE.md.\n  (d) Publish `walk_verdict` wherever `analysis_method` is published and let\n      consumers key on the finer axis. Cost: every consumer changes.\n\nDO NOT CLOSE THIS BY ARGUING. Measure first: how many findings across the\ncorpus sit at not_attempted, and WHY the walk was not attempted for them\n(INV-zidur's closure note lists the guards above the walk that can fail with\nfn_has_ddg still true: sink_node != source_fn, no source call lines, no sink\ncall lines, source not tracked, sink lexically before source). If one guard\ndominates, that guard -- not the label -- may be the thing to fix.\n\nNOT A REGRESSION FROM WI-ripas. Before it these findings were `structural` for\nthe WRONG reason (a key mismatch that discarded real data). They are now\n`ddg_mixed` for a defensible-but-coarse reason. The label question predates\nWI-ripas; WI-ripas only made the affected population large enough to matter."  # 7845
    fields: {}  # 7845
- op: discuss  # 49e5
  at: '2026-09-22T23:52:59Z'  # 49e5
  by: agent  # 49e5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 49e5
  clock: 2  # 49e5
  nonce: '49e5'  # 49e5
  message: "MEASURED FIRST, as the row asked. Census, measurement 0007's method (verify-claims --format json, generic-taint-claims.yaml, unit = evidence row), on 0007's 11-repo cohort plus sherpa-onnx and podman-compose. Analyzer pinned: dev 4610d2d693 in a worktree, PYTHONHASHSEED=0. An earlier unpinned run was byte-identical in totals. Artifacts: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dopat_census_pinned/.\n\n            rows  confirmed  escaped  NOT_ATTEMPTED  unavailable  unconfirmed\n  default    498        50       40            242          166            0\n  nonprod    878        61       74            551          192            0\n\nnot_attempted is 242 of 282 ddg_mixed rows (85.8%) on the default arm and 551 of 625 (88.2%) on nonprod. So the row's worry is real at scale: most ddg_mixed rows got a DDG-flavoured label from coverage with no walk.\n\nWHY NOT ATTEMPTED (first blocker; partitions, do not add):\n  default   cross_function 151 (62.4%)   sink_before_source 55 (22.7%)   source_not_tracked 36 (14.9%)\n  nonprod   cross_function 366 (66.4%)   sink_before_source 113 (20.5%)  source_not_tracked 72 (13.1%)\ncross_function dominates. It is §3a's by-construction intraprocedural limit, fixable only by §4 summaries, so the row's \"if one guard dominates, fix the guard\" does not apply to the dominant one.\n\nOPTION (d) IS ALREADY SHIPPED, which the row did not know. walk_verdict is published on every JSON evidence row. The text view prints \"§3a walk verdicts for those findings: ...\" directly under the analysis_method line, plus a paragraph stating that not_attempted is ignorance, not absence.\n\nWHAT IS STILL WRONG, and FIXED in this row's PR: docs/VERIFY-CLAIMS-SCOPE.md defined `ddg_mixed` as \"the walk ran and did not confirm\". That is false for 86-88% of the rows carrying it.\n\nA SECOND GUARD IS WORTH AN OWNER DECISION (see WI-mojaz for the adjudication). On the pretix nonprod arm, a seeded sample adjudicated with 0022's classifier (control: reproduces 0022's 119/119 verdicts) puts sink_before_source situations at 22 FP / 0 TP (+6 vacuous). Treating sink_before_source as refutation would be a removal rule, and ADR-0052 makes §3a refutation confirm-only. So that is an ADR-level ruling, not mine. Soundness caveat: a loop can carry a later source to an earlier sink.\n\nLABEL (options a-c): left as INV-zidur ruled. Remapping is still the owner's call. The measurement says the collapse is 86-88%, and (d) already discloses it on both surfaces."  # 49e5
